  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nExpansive long wave trough across eastern North America will\ndeamplify and lift out early next week. This will allow ridging to \ndevelop into the region with the ridge axis passing across the area \non Wednesday. \n\nCyclonic low level flow will finally move off to the east as high\npressure starts to build in tomorrow. The high will move across the\nregion on Monday. As it heads east, southerly flow will become\nestablished by midweek. \n\nClouds will clear out for a period of time this morning but then\nredevelop this afternoon and persist into Sunday night. Then skies\nwill become mainly clear from Monday into Wednesday. Some clouds\nmight spread into the region during the latter part of the week.\n\nTemperatures will remain below normal through the weekend. Daytime\ntemperatures will then warm through the week. But with a dry airmass,\nthere will be a big diurnal range each day, so lows will still fall\nto near or below freezing until late next week.",
